,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"5.42\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-[3px]\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"linear-gradient(to bottom, #f59e0b, #f59e0b33)\",\"boxShadow\":\"0 0 12px -2px #f59e0b80\"}}],\"$L9f\",\"$La0\"]}],\"$La1\",\"$La2\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The one thing that makes Nolan work\"]}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Nolan's solo skills are deliberately undertuned. Expansion's raw hit lands weaker than most level-4 marksman autos. The real damage is Dimensional Rift, the passive: whenever two rifts touch, they detonate, pull enemies to the intersection, and deal a separate chunk of physical damage on top of the cast that placed them. Every rift is temporary and slows anything touching it, so the hero's entire job is to place two of them on the same target before the first one expires.\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"That inverts how you play an assassin. Normal burst heroes land a stun, then press everything, then walk away. Nolan enters a fight with no damage on the board, spends his first cast and his dash to lay the first rift, and only starts dealing damage on the second cast. That is why supports and marksmen who would die in one rotation to Gusion can often kite a full Nolan combo: the combo has a setup beat.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Three kit quirks matter more than the numbers. Cosmic Leap is the enhanced dash basic Nolan gets after a stretch of not dealing or taking hero damage, which means the first engage of every fight comes free from fog of war with a rift already placed on the target. Expansion leaves its rift on the first enemy hit, so poking a minion wave burns the cast without placing the rift where you need it. Fracture purges all debuffs on Nolan the moment it activates, which makes it a reactive cleanse against CC chains that were already chained onto him, not a preemptive shield.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The first four minutes: clear, spike, gank\"]}]\n83:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Nolan clears fast because every skill places a rift and S2's cooldown is short enough to chain through camps. Follow the order below. Do not improvise.\"}]\n84:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Take S2 first, walk to red buff, open the clear with S1 + S2 + auto.\"}],\" S1 places a rift on the first camp unit hit, S2 dashes through and places a second rift, the two rifts overlap in the small camp radius and detonate through the whole stack. Red buff dies in one rotation with retribution timed on the camp leader. Full HP, roughly 18 seconds to next camp.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Cross to the two small camps and the scuttle, then invade blue.\"}],\" Skill 1 at level 2, then the lite version of the same rotation. By the time you back, you are level 4 with Roam Boots or the Retribution component plus a second item's worth of gold.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"First gank at the 2:30 mark on the side lane that pushed first.\"}],\" Walk in from the river brush with Cosmic Leap charged. The enhanced basic dashes onto the target and drops the first rift; S1 in the opposite direction of their flash places the second rift behind them so the intersection pulls them back toward you, not away. If they Flicker the pull, the combo still connects because the rift detonation tracks them for the delay window.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Burn Flicker only to cover a failed gank or to jump a wall after you secured a kill. Do not use it to close distance on the first engage. Cosmic Leap already is your gap close, and wasting Flicker to \\\"double-dash in\\\" leaves you with nothing if the target has one more escape than you expected.\"}]\n86:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The two-item spike at five minutes\"]}]\n87:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Nolan's fighting identity comes online when \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/items/blade-of-the-heptaseas\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Blade of the Heptaseas\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-1\",{\"href\":\"/items/hunter-strike\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Hunter Strike\"}],\" are both complete, typically around the 5- to 6-minute mark with retribution-boosted farm. Before that spike, his burst is camp-clearing damage at best. After it, an undefended marksman dies inside one rotation.\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Heptaseas is the key item and the reason. Its Ambush passive primes the next basic attack after a no-damage window, and that window is the exact same one that arms Cosmic Leap. The two effects trigger on the same basic attack. A level-7 Nolan walking out of the river bush lands a Cosmic Leap enhanced basic that stacks the Heptaseas Ambush bonus and drops a rift; S2 dashes through and drops the second rift; the intersection pulls and detonates. The detonation adds damage to the opening attack and dash before you cast S1.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Hunter Strike does two things at once. The cooldown reduction keeps S2 ready to dash twice per teamfight window, so a cleansed rift can be replaced. The Retribution passive (confusingly named, not the jungle spell) grants a big burst of movement speed after landing consecutive hits, which stacks with the slow from Heptaseas' Ambush and turns Nolan into the fastest hero on the map in the middle of a brawl. The chase problem solves itself.\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"$La3\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8b:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning: engage first, not last\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The reflex on an assassin is to let the initiator go in and clean up when the carries overextend. That reflex will get Nolan killed. His combo needs a stretch of no damage to prime Cosmic Leap and Heptaseas, which only happens from fog of war, not mid-teamfight. If Nolan is the third hero to enter a fight that already started, both primers are already broken.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Three rules.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Engage from a flank before the main fight starts.\"}],\" Ideal timing is when the enemy mid and jungler are rotating to an objective but the fight has not yet committed. Enter from brush with Cosmic Leap charged, one-shot whichever squishy walked closest to your side, then disengage with Fracture's backward dash. This is a single pick, not a teamfight; your team cleans up 5v4.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Do not tunnel the ultimate purge onto the first CC you see.\"}],\" Fracture is a cleanse, not a preemptive shield. If you pop it the moment a Khufra ball is in the air, you still eat the knockup (skill was in progress). Save it for a chain: first CC lands, you purge it mid-chain to avoid the second CC (a Saber ult, a Ruby pull, a Chou suppression followup).\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Target priority is whoever is farthest from their support.\"}],\" Nolan's damage needs a clean combo window. A 99-percentile Khimer with Estes heal-stacked behind him is a bad target; the Harley 2 screens up who stepped off creep for a ward is the correct target, even if the Harley is 5 items.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Your support matters more than people admit. If it is Estes, you can push the pick one layer deeper than safe because the heal covers your return. If it is Diggie, you get zero peel outside of Time Journey, so the first time you engage from brush is also the last pick you get that fight; make it count.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: two locked slots, four real decisions\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Two items are not negotiable: a \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/items/ice-retribution\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"jungle boot\"}],\" (Ice Retribution in most drafts, discussed below) and \",\"$La4\",\". The other four slots are actual conversations.\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$La5\",\"\\n\",\"$La6\",\"\\n\",\"$La7\",\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\"]\n8c:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Nolan\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8d:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 bg-surface-3\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6b\",null,{\"src\":\"https://akmweb.youngjoygame.com/web/svnres/img/test/homepage_2_2_16_1232_1/100_6bbfac806f29d29f17fea9e98d2d2fee.png\",\"alt\":\"Saber - Wandering Sword\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"priority\":\"$undefined\",\"fetchPriority\":\"$undefined\",\"fill\":true,\"className\":\"object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300\",\"sizes\":\"56px\",\"placeholder\":\"blur\",\"blurDataURL\":\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj48cmVjdCB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgZmlsbD0iIzBkMTIyNSIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex-1 min-w-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading font-bold text-text-primary group-hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors truncate\",\"children\":\"Saber\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2 mt-0.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"class